A||||6||Scott_M||Manual Transaxle||||1||
Z||000000||Scott_M||02-15-2001||01:21 AM||||Whats the procedure for draining the Manual Transaxle? I've checked the Haynes/Chilton manuals and they only go over the draining of the automatics. Is it the same? It's for an 87 SE manual 5 spd.4 cyl.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Signature.jpg">   <BR>87 SE 4cyl,5 spd. manual||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||02-15-2001||01:33 AM||||Open drain plug, let drain, replace drain plug!! Some have a dipstick that you can remove to refill, if not, you will need to remove the speedo sender to fill.  NOW WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO FILL IT UP WITH? There is much debate over this. Your owners manual may say engine oil or ATF, but late in the fiero production, GM, Changed the recomended fluid to GM synchromesh. Cost about 10 bucks a quart and my getrag takes 2 quarts.  The Izusu holds a diferent amount. I would at least use 5w30 synthetic engine oil or the GM product from the dealer.<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||02-15-2001||07:07 AM||||Be VERY CAREFUL when you remove the speed sensor sending unit from the 4spd Mincie to check the oil.  The plastic gear on the sending unit is only slightly smaller than the opening in the gearcase and needs to be removed very carefully or else the gear can be knocked off and fall into the gearbox.||||reg||1
Z||000003||montage||02-15-2001||09:14 AM||||I went to my local quick lube place (Pennzoil dealer) and purchased Pennzoil synchromesh for $4.00 a quart. Same as GM lube but cheaper. My understanding is the big benefit of synchromesh is improved lubrication of non-ferrous parts. Shifts smoother.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||02-15-2001||10:13 AM||||I use ATF in both of my Getrags, and they shift very well. Much better than what was in them before (I don't really know).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Scott_M||02-15-2001||06:42 PM||||I was thinking of using the synchromesh. She's got 116,00 mi on it already, and I want as much "preventative" maintainence done, as humanly ($$$) possible. <BR>Thanks guys<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Signature.jpg">   <BR>87 SE 4cyl,5 spd. manual||||reg||1
Z||000006||Scott_M||02-17-2001||05:09 PM||||Neither Pep Boys or Autozone had the Synchromesh fluid, pennzoil or otherwise, though there was a Castrol synthethic 5w-30. Would this be simmiliar?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Signature.jpg">   <BR>87 SE 4cyl,5 spd. manual||||reg||1
